<!-- WHAT MAKES A STRONG SESSION -->
<section>
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What Makes a Strong DLF Forum Session?</h2>

        <div class="mt-8 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

            <div class="border rounded-xl p-5">
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Participatory</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Sessions should actively involve participants through discussion, collaboration, and shared exploration.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="border rounded-xl p-5">
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Inclusive</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Welcome diverse perspectives, experience levels, and institutional contexts.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="border rounded-xl p-5">
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Action-Oriented</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Provide clear takeaways participants can apply in their own work.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

        <p class="mt-6 text-gray-700 max-w-3xl">
            We also welcome presentations from the commercial sector that contribute
            knowledge, lessons learned, and community value rather than promoting specific products.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

